<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of German-Austria</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1919 CE · capital Vienna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived first Austrian republic of 1918-19, created from the German-speaking lands of the Habsburg monarchy and seeking union with Germany.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> dissolved, the German-speaking members of the Imperial Council formed a provisional national assembly on 21 October 1918. On 12 November 1918, the day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-i">Emperor Charles I</a> withdrew from government, it proclaimed the Republic of German-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, declaring it part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">German Republic</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-renner">Karl Renner</a> of the Social Democrats led the government as state chancellor. The republic claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudetenland">Sudetenland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-tyrol">South Tyrol</a> and other German-speaking areas, but could not enforce these claims. It faced hunger, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a>, returning soldiers and a communist putsch attempt, and abolished the nobility and banished the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in April 1919.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-germain-en-laye-1919">Treaty of Saint-Germain</a> in September 1919 forbade union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and set <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria's</a> borders. On 21 October 1919 the state was renamed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-austrian-republic">Republic of Austria</a>, the First Austrian Republic.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-german-austria.jpg" alt="Republic of German-Austria" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: SpinnerLaserzthe2nd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Austria_(1230%E2%80%931934,_1945%E2%80%932000).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vienna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karl Renner, Karl Seitz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Deutschösterreich, German-Austria</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=republic-of-german-austria" aria-label="Republic of German-Austria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5061 491 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of German-Austria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5381 747L5380 747M5381 747L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5380 747h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 747h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vienna. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=republic-of-german-austria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
